{
  "name": "Evotec palette v1 (Graphite)",
  "decision": "D14, owner, 2026-09-26",
  "source": "Palette study candidate C; contrast and CVD checks in plan section 8.3",
  "notes": [
    "Severity has a fill (marks, bars, dots) and an ink (text on surfaces and tinted chips). Every ink is at least 4.5:1 on the card surface and on a 13% tint of its fill.",
    "Outcome 'fail' has no colour of its own: a failed result is coloured by its severity.",
    "Operational state maps onto the same hues: up=outcome.pass, degraded=severity.medium, down=severity.critical, recovering=severity.low, maintenance=state.maintenance, notObservable and unknown=outcome.neutral with hatching.",
    "Series colours are used in this fixed order and never for status. Past six series, charts switch to small multiples. Validated against the Graphite card surfaces: worst adjacent CVD delta E 10.6 (light, surface #ffffff) and 12.6 (dark, surface #16181c); worst adjacent normal-vision delta E 15.9 (light) and 16.1 (dark); lightness band, chroma and 3:1 contrast pass in both modes.",
    "Ramps (optional in consumers): arrays run from weakest to strongest magnitude. 'sequential' is one hue (blue) for magnitude and counts, with no status meaning. 'diverging' has a negative arm (red), a neutral midpoint and a positive arm (blue), each arm weakest to strongest. Every ramp passed the ordinal checks (monotone lightness, adjacent delta L >= 0.06, weakest step >= 2:1 on the card surface, single hue) in its mode."
  ],
